    "rich_text_standard": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "f_sub": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Eating it raw",
            "subheading_size": "subtitle-md",
            "secondary_color": true
          }
        },
        "f_head": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What sashimi-grade means to us",
            "heading_size": "title-md",
            "heading_tag": "h2",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "f_text": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>There is no official or regulated definition of &ldquo;sashimi-grade&rdquo; or &ldquo;sushi-grade&rdquo; fish in the United States. Sellers use the terms to signal that fish is safe to eat raw, but they are not a certification or a legal standard. So here is ours.</p><p>All of our seafood is vacuum sealed and blast frozen to -10 &deg;F at peak freshness, which preserves taste, texture and colour, and is processed in an accredited facility. It is lab tested for mercury and microplastics. Farmed fish raised on formulated feed are exempt from the FDA Food Code&rsquo;s parasite-freezing rule, and we blast-freeze at harvest anyway. That is what sashimi-grade means to us.</p><p>There is always some risk in eating anything raw or undercooked. If you are concerned or particularly sensitive, consult your doctor. The FDA conservatively suggests cooking to an internal temperature of 145 &deg;F.</p>",
            "text_size": "subtext-md",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_font": "body",
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "f_btn": {
          "type": "button",
          "settings": {
            "button_label": "How we source it",
            "button_link": "/pages/why-clean-seafood-matters",
            "button_style": "secondary",
            "button_size": "md",
            "button_external": false,
            "button_icon": true
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "f_sub",
        "f_head",
        "f_text",
        "f_btn"
      ],
